# Roteiro de demonstração da Wallet Ledger API.
# Suba a API com `docker compose up --build` e execute as requisições em ordem
# (VS Code com a extensão REST Client, ou Rider).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Login da Ana (conta de demonstração)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ana@walletledger.dev", "password": "Demo@1234" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 2. Saldo
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/account
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. Conferir o destinatário antes do PIX (nome e CPF mascarados)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/pix/keys/lookup?type=email&value=bruno@walletledger.dev
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. PIX de R$ 25,90 para o Bruno
# Rode duas vezes sem mudar a chave: o dinheiro só sai uma vez.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transfers/pix
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-pix-0001

{ "keyType": "email", "keyValue": "bruno@walletledger.dev", "amountCents": 2590, "description": "Almoço" }

### 5. Extrato (página de 10)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/account/statement?limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Minhas chaves PIX
# @name keys
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/pix/keys
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. QR code de cobrança de R$ 10,00 (texto do "Pix Copia e Cola")
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/pix/charges
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "keyId": "{{keys.response.body.$[0].id}}", "amountCents": 1000 }

### 8. Saldo insuficiente → 422 insufficient_funds
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/transfers/pix
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-pix-sem-saldo

{ "keyType": "email", "keyValue": "bruno@walletledger.dev", "amountCents": 999999999 }
